From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoBench <neobench@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] build: reserve m68k/NeoBench target in stable/15

This patch is the first build-system hook for the NeoBench 68060 port. It
intentionally does not claim that the upstream FreeBSD tree has native m68k
support; the machine-dependent sources supplied by NeoBench must be installed
before the kernel target can be built.

---
 Makefile.inc1 | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/Makefile.inc1
+++ b/Makefile.inc1
@@ -132,6 +132,7 @@ TARGET_TRIPLE?=${TARGET_ARCH:S/amd64/x86_64/}-${TARGET_TRIPLE_ABI}-freebsd${OS_REVISION}
 KNOWN_ARCHES?=\taarch64/arm64 \\
 \t\tamd64 \\
 \t\tarmv7/arm \\
 \t\ti386 \\
 \t\tpowerpc \\
 \t\tpowerpc64/powerpc \\
 \t\tpowerpc64le/powerpc \\
-\t\triscv64/riscv
+\t\triscv64/riscv \\
+\t\tm68k/m68k
 
*** End Patch
